# Scenario: the cube-mapped material under the Vulkan validation layer (M11.1b, B-008; docs/M11_PLAN.md section 26):
# the metal slime -- the one material that samples a cube map (the engine's default cube, unit 3), a program whose
# translation declares each texture unit on its own binding -- created beside the hero on field 14 (the tools' `spawn`,
# the game's own set-up) and drawn; then the map entered again with the scripts' random forced so every slime spawn
# point shows one. PS3RECOMP_VK_VALIDATION=1: tests/devtools_suite.py fails on any validation error (B-008 was a
# descriptor layout without the per-unit bindings: "viewType must match the Dim operand", "descriptor set in layout
# must match the shader"), and keeps the pictures. Needs the Khronos validation layer (the Vulkan SDK); without it the
# check says so.
#! saves build/checkpoints/castle-front
#! env DOTHEROES_DEVELOPER_MODE=1 DOTHEROES_NATIVE_CD=1 DOTHEROES_NATIVE_SOLVER=1,2,4,5,6 GCM_WRAP_LAP=1
#! env DOTHEROES_PRESENT_ONCE=1 DOTHEROES_DEV_STATE=1 PS3_VERBOSE=0 SHOT_EVERY=0 DUMP=1 PS3RECOMP_VK_VALIDATION=1
#! secs 600

include common.drive

log TitleMovie 120
sleep 5
call continue
state life>0,area==17 90
sleep 3
dev nodeath on
dev invulnerable on
dev warp Field_14 -gDebug @150
sleep 3
dev spawn HagureSlime 2.4 0
sleep 0.5
shot slime
sleep 1
shot slime-b
dev enemies
dev lua __devtools_random=math.random; math.random=function(a,b) if b then return a elseif a then return 1 else return 0 end end
dev respawn @150
sleep 2
dev lua math.random=__devtools_random; __devtools_random=nil
shot forced
sleep 3
shot forced-b
dev coverage
